        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/45deac/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-15T12:39:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>On page 17 of 5th edition Spirit island in the rule book it says no part of a card may be skipped, its \"all or nothing\"</p>\n<p>So imagine the set up of the board (D) with 3 Dihan on the #2Grass Land and 3 Dihan in the #5 mountain land. (#2 is adjacent to #5)</p>\n<p>Now with the card \"call to migrate\" I have the option to \"gather up to 3 Dihan\" then \"push up to 3 Dihan\":&nbsp;</p>\n<p>So naturally I can do the action: Gather 3 Dihan from Land #2 into Land#5 THEN Push 3 Dihan from Land #5 into say Land #1.</p>\n<p>But can I instead do the action: \"Gather&nbsp;0&nbsp;Dihan\" from Land #2 into Land #5 and&nbsp;then chose to push 3 Dihan in the land #1&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Because it says \"up to 3\" so I assume \"up to 3\" can mean \"0\" and thus doing this forfills the requiremnt of both actions being comepleted</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:55:10.640Z",
